cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CDaLCqr in your work, please cite this repository and the methodological references listed in DESCRIPTION."
title: "CDaLCqr: coordinate descent for high-dimensional longitudinal quantile regression with compositional covariates"
abstract: >-
  An R package that estimates penalized quantile regression models for
  longitudinal compositional covariates. Locally adaptive weights are built
  from a Belloni-Chernozhukov pilot fit, the smoothed check loss is used for
  estimation, and the tuning parameter is selected by the generalized
  information criterion. The package supports the adaptive lasso, MCP and SCAD
  penalties and uses exact inactive-coordinate screening in its C++ kernels.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Linhui
version: 0.1.0
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: https://github.com/density04/CDaLCqr
url: https://github.com/density04/CDaLCqr
keywords:
  - quantile regression
  - compositional data
  - high-dimensional statistics
  - coordinate descent
